CA_EVENT \"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/adapters/runners/python.py:9:    harness_instructions = \"Use Python imports from the current isolated workspace and print CA_EVENT JSON containing actual returned values.\"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md:5:CORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias explicitly selects the declared harness prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is owed. It is not the first prerequisite by array order. Harness.prerequisites contains prerequisite events only; monitors select independent result events. ObservableProperty.identity_fields declares the stable operation identity once, using fields present at the relevant observation points. Do not repeat a result as a prerequisite or duplicate each identity equality as a Comparison. Reference conditions declare necessary predecessor relationships; unrelated prerequisites have no implicit list order. Assertions may refer to any declared prerequisite alias that actually precedes the result. Missing identity/reference fields or nonunique associations remain unknown. Independent applicability is checked before requiring unrelated history. Alias-dependent applicability follows correlation. Each operation is matched separately. A complete violating witness survives missing results in demonstrably independent operations, while coverage remains partial. Same-witness ambiguity and potentially global parse loss still block attribution. Use independent identity, not the compared value, to associate an input and output. A context expected to change cannot also be an equality filter. More complex histories need actual correlated prerequisites and results; unsupported general temporal expressions remain a stated limitation.\n109:\tcallStats inMemStorageCallStats\n122:\tms.callStats.initialState++\n138:\tms.callStats.entries++\n162:\tms.callStats.term++\n177:\tms.callStats.lastIndex+